# Browser
# Heartless Act in the browser: its second mode asks which counters of the three on Bot2's Ornithopter come off, "up to" three, with a
# caption that says so (it is an effect, not a cost). Bot1 takes the flying and the first strike counter and leaves the lifelink counter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Abigale, Eloquent First-Year
Heartless Act
Ornithopter
Plains
Plains
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Plains x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Abigale, Eloquent First-Year.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Flying = 1
Bot1.Hand.Heartless Act.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Remove up to three counters)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Heartless Act: remove up to 3 counters
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Detail = Any kinds, as many as you choose, or none  ·  0 of up to 3 chosen  ·  click a permanent to take one of its counters, or a button below
Bot1.RemoveCounters(Ornithopter: Flying 1; Ornithopter: FirstStrike 1)

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Flying = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.FirstStrike = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Lifelink = 1
Stack.Count = 0
